  "code": "def factor_downside_semivariance_ema8(df):\n    \"\"\"Smooth trailing concentration of realized variance from negative returns.\"\"\"\n    df_copy = df.copy()\n    ret = df_copy[\"close\"].pct_change()\n    downside_var = ret.clip(upper=0.0).pow(2).rolling(20, min_periods=20).mean()\n    total_var = ret.pow(2).rolling(20, min_periods=20).mean()\n    downside_share = downside_var / total_var.replace(0.0, np.nan)\n    df_copy[\"factor_downside_semivariance_ema8\"] = downside_share.ewm(span=8, adjust=False, min_periods=8).mean()\n    return df_copy[\"factor_downside_semivariance_ema8\"]",
  "cross_sectional_rationale": "Downside-variance concentration is most informative relative to same-day peers because crash fragility is a cross-sectional characteristic. Robust standardization limits the influence of extreme stress observations while retaining relative exposure.",
